WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.896 --> 00:00:08.560
Diego Alvarez: Morning, Greg. Morning, Raj. How's Phoenix treating you? Still hot?

2
00:00:09.343 --> 00:00:16.266
Greg Hollis: Yeah, we're in that fake fall window. Ninety-eight yesterday, supposed to be a hundred and one tomorrow.

3
00:00:16.759 --> 00:00:26.469
Raj Malhotra: Uh, I was in Vegas Monday and Tuesday. Same thing. The AC in the Henderson store went out, so I spent most of Tuesday in a conference room there.

4
00:00:27.261 --> 00:00:29.561
Diego Alvarez: Oh man. Did it get fixed?

5
00:00:30.326 --> 00:00:36.595
Raj Malhotra: Wednesday morning. The tech was there at seven. Um, it was fine, just a compressor thing.

6
00:00:37.255 --> 00:00:41.937
Greg Hollis: Okay so, agenda-wise, Diego, I know you had a couple of uh, things.

7
00:00:42.219 --> 00:00:52.150
Diego Alvarez: Yeah, mostly logistics. Let me pull up my notes here. You know, Um, one thing I wanted to check on is the Q4 training dates.

8
00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:58.505
Diego Alvarez: I know we talked about getting the BDC folks on a refresher before the holiday push.

9
00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:02.542
Greg Hollis: Right. So that's Raj's area more than mine.

10
00:01:03.591 --> 00:01:11.537
Raj Malhotra: I mean, yeah. We've got about forty people in the BDC across the rooftops. What were the dates you were thinking?

11
00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:22.980
Diego Alvarez: I had two windows held. First is October 14th and 15th, second is the 21st and 22nd. Um, Both are Tuesdays like, and Wednesdays, two hours each morning.

12
00:01:24.166 --> 00:01:35.977
Raj Malhotra: The 14th and and 15th is better. The 21st we've got a regional managers meeting in Tucson, so half the room would be on a laptop in a hotel.

13
00:01:37.017 --> 00:01:48.475
Diego Alvarez: Okay, let's lock the 14th and 15th. Do you want me to send the calendar holds to you and Greg, or should I go straight to the BDC leads?

14
00:01:49.112 --> 00:01:57.373
Raj Malhotra: Send to me first. I'll forward. There's a couple of new team leads I want to make sure actually show up.

15
00:01:58.142 --> 00:02:04.274
Diego Alvarez: Got it. And is it still the same group of forty, or has that changed?

16
00:02:05.655 --> 00:02:17.496
Raj Malhotra: It's thirty-eight now. Two people moved over to the service side in August. And we picked up one at the Scottsdale store, so, you know, net minus one.

17
00:02:18.436 --> 00:02:25.201
Greg Hollis: Sorry, hold on. Raj, was that the the Scottsdale BDC hire, the one that started Labor Day week?

18
00:02:25.863 --> 00:02:30.297
Raj Malhotra: Yeah. You know, she came over from the internet sales desk there.

19
00:02:30.739 --> 00:02:35.945
Greg Hollis: Okay. I just wanted to make sure I wasn't double counting her.

20
00:02:36.988 --> 00:02:49.270
Diego Alvarez: Um, no problem. I'll put thirty-eight on the invite and we can adjust. Um, the other thing, user changes. I got a ticket that one of your marketing coordinators left in early September?

21
00:02:49.479 --> 00:02:56.467
Greg Hollis: Yeah, that's right. Her last day was the 11th. You know, we haven't backfilled yet. Probably posting it next week.

22
00:02:57.833 --> 00:03:04.458
Diego Alvarez: Okay. Do you want me to deactivate her access now, or leave it until the replacement starts?

23
00:03:05.783 --> 00:03:10.496
Greg Hollis: Deactivate now. Raj can tell you, we're pretty strict about that.

24
00:03:11.602 --> 00:03:15.790
Raj Malhotra: Yeah, please do. Finance gets twitchy about active accounts with no owner.

25
00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:20.607
Diego Alvarez: Makes sense. Um, I'll do that today and send you a confirmation.

26
00:03:21.508 --> 00:03:22.308
Raj Malhotra: Appreciate it.

27
00:03:23.045 --> 00:03:32.123
Diego Alvarez: Last one from me, and this is just me being nosy about planning. What does your call volume look like heading into October?

28
00:03:32.123 --> 00:03:37.254
Diego Alvarez: I'm trying to get ahead of any support coverage gaps on my side.

29
00:03:37.457 --> 00:03:49.330
Greg Hollis: Historically we see um, a bump the second week of October, then it flattens until Black Friday. Last year October was up, what, eleven percent over September?

30
00:03:50.632 --> 00:03:54.689
Raj Malhotra: Somewhere in there. I'd have to pull the actual number.

31
00:03:56.009 --> 00:04:01.994
Greg Hollis: Don't hold me to eleven. It was a real bump, that's all I remember.

32
00:04:02.206 --> 00:04:08.643
Diego Alvarez: That's helpful enough. I mean, I'll just make sure my coverage is normal through that stretch.

33
00:04:09.277 --> 00:04:17.374
Raj Malhotra: And the holiday hours kick in the week of Thanksgiving, so the BDC schedule shifts. I'll send you that once it's final.

34
00:04:17.988 --> 00:04:20.929
Diego Alvarez: Perfect. Anything from you two before we wrap?

35
00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:27.632
Greg Hollis: Nope, I think we're good. Everything on our end is just steady. Thanks for the training dates.

36
00:04:28.744 --> 00:04:30.026
Raj Malhotra: Same. Thanks, Diego.

37
00:04:31.511 --> 00:04:39.087
Diego Alvarez: Great. I'll send the invite today and the deactivation confirmation. Talk to you both in a couple weeks. Stay cool out there.

38
00:04:39.825 --> 00:04:40.836
Greg Hollis: Ha. We'll try.
